  "id": "persuasive-communication",
  "term": "persuasive communication",
  "definition": "Persuasive communication is communication intended to shape attitudes, and its impact can vary depending on how well the message’s emotional or thinking-focused content matches the recipient’s usual orientation. In this research context, attitudes were more influenced by the emotional tone of a message when it matched a person’s stronger affective orientation.",
